{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Python 3 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++17 code to Python 3 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++17 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include<bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nconst int MOD = 1000000007;\nint add(int a, int b) { return (a += b) >= MOD ? a - MOD : a; }\nint mul(int a, int b) { return (long long)a * b % MOD; }\nint sub(int a, int b) { return (a -= b) < 0 ? a + MOD : a; }\nint power(int a, int b) { int r=1; for(; b; b>>=1) { if(b&1) r=mul(r,a); a=mul(a,a); } return r; }\nint lowbit(int x) { return x & -x; }\n\nint n;\nint prob[10][10];\nint q[10][128];\nint dp[10][70010];\nint ch[70010][128];\nmap<bitset<128>, int> id;\nint idcnt = 0;\n\nint dfs(bitset<128> s) {\n    if(id.count(s)) return id[s];\n    id[s] = ++idcnt;\n    for(int m=0; m<(1<<n); ++m) {\n        bitset<128> t = s;\n        for(int j=0; j<(1<<n); ++j) {\n            if(!t[j]) {\n                int x = m & j;\n                while(x) {\n                    int lb = lowbit(x);\n                    if(s[j ^ lb]) {\n                        t[j] = 1;\n                        break;\n                    }\n                    x -= lb;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        ch[id[s]][m] = dfs(t);\n    }\n    return id[s];\n}\n\nint main() {\n    cin >> n;\n    dfs(1);\n    for(int i=0; i<n; ++i)\n        for(int j=0; j<n; ++j) {\n            cin >> prob[i][j];\n            prob[i][j] = mul(prob[i][j], power(100, MOD-2));\n        }\n    for(int i=0; i<n; ++i) {\n        for(int j=0; j<(1<<n); ++j) {\n            q[i][j] = 1;\n            for(int k=0; k<n; ++k) {\n                if((j>>k)&1) q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], prob[i][k]);\n                else q[i][j] = mul(q[i][j], sub(1, prob[i][k]));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    dp[0][1] = 1;\n    for(int i=1; i<=n; ++i) {\n        for(int j=1; j<=idcnt; ++j) {\n            for(int m=0; m<(1<<n); ++m) {\n                int to = ch[j][m];\n                dp[i][to] = add(dp[i][to], mul(dp[i-1][j], q[i-1][m]));\n            }\n        }\n    }\n    bitset<128> full;\n    for(int i=0; i<(1<<n); ++i) full[i] = 1;\n    cout << dp[n][id[full]] << endl;\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport sys\nsys.setrecursionlimit(1000000)\n\nMOD = 1000000007\n\ndef add(a, b):\n    a += b\n    if a >= MOD:\n        a -= MOD\n    return a\n\ndef mul(a, b):\n    return (a * b) % MOD\n\ndef sub(a, b):\n    a -= b\n    if a < 0:\n        a += MOD\n    return a\n\ndef power(a, b):\n    r = 1\n    while b:\n        if b & 1:\n            r = mul(r, a)\n        a = mul(a, a)\n        b >>= 1\n    return r\n\ndef lowbit(x):\n    return x & -x\n\nn = int(input())\nprob = [[0]*n for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n):\n    row = list(map(int, input().split()))\n    for j in range(n):\n        prob[i][j] = mul(row[j], power(100, MOD-2))\n\n# compute q[i][m]\nq = [[0]*(1<<n) for _ in range(n)]\nfor i in range(n):\n    for m in range(1<<n):\n        val = 1\n        for k in range(n):\n            if (m >> k) & 1:\n                val = mul(val, prob[i][k])\n            else:\n                val = mul(val, sub(1, prob[i][k]))\n        q[i][m] = val\n\n# global state for dfs\nid_map = {}  # bitset -> id\nidcnt = 0\nch = [None]  # index 0 unused, ch[id] is list of size (1<<n)\n\ndef dfs(s):\n    global idcnt, ch\n    if s in id_map:\n        return id_map[s]\n    idcnt += 1\n    id_map[s] = idcnt\n    # allocate ch for this id\n    ch.append([0]*(1<<n))\n    cur_id = idcnt\n    for m in range(1<<n):\n        t = s\n        for j in range(1<<n):\n            if not ((t >> j) & 1):\n                x = m & j\n                while x:\n                    lb = lowbit(x)\n                    if (s >> (j ^ lb)) & 1:\n                        t |= (1 << j)\n                        break\n                    x -= lb\n        ch[cur_id][m] = dfs(t)\n    return cur_id\n\n# initial bitset: only bit 0 set? Actually dfs(1) means bitset with only bit 0 set? In C++, bitset<128> s; s[0]=1? Actually they call dfs(1) which is integer 1, so bit 0 set. So we pass integer 1.\ndfs(1)\n\n# dp: (n+1) x (idcnt+1) initialized to 0\ndp = [[0]*(idcnt+1) for _ in range(n+1)]\ndp[0][1] = 1  # id of bitset 1 is 1\n\nfor i in range(1, n+1):\n    for j in range(1, idcnt+1):\n        if dp[i-1][j] == 0:\n            continue\n        for m in range(1<<n):\n            to = ch[j][m]\n            dp[i][to] = add(dp[i][to], mul(dp[i-1][j], q[i-1][m]))\n\n# full bitset: all bits from 0 to (1<<n)-1 set\nfull = (1 << (1<<n)) - 1\nprint(dp[n][id_map[full]])\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.95\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-5.590759246842936e-05, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.0002783149539027363, -0.05505911633372307, -1.1920928244535389e-07, -0.014167092740535736, -0.008410155773162842, 0.0, 0.0, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, 0.0, -0.012537943199276924, -0.3868710994720459, -0.005847016349434853, -0.20147453248500824, -3.099436753473128e-06, -1.1920928244535389e-07, 0.0, -2.8967437174287625e-05, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.004078642465174198, -5.125986263010418e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.7418097943154862e-06, -5.